From cbae07ee57a0bc452af0a28095b08135bdf9b2b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:07:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U29: /writing asks for the shelf only (both API runtimes)

posts.listPublished takes an optional { slugs, since }. With either field
it returns only the rows named by slug, or whose essay date (publishedAt,
else createdAt: the shelf's Latest rule) is at or after `since`, in the
listing's order; with neither, the full listing as before.

- server/posts-listing.ts: the zod input and pickListing for the dev router.
- server/routers.ts: listPublished takes the input and applies it.
- api/index.ts: pickListing, applied in both handlers (trpcHandler and the
  batch processProc). Malformed fields are ignored there.
- client/src/lib/shelf.ts: shelfListingInput(), the live shelf slugs and
  the Latest cutoff.
- client/src/pages/Writing.tsx: asks with shelfListingInput() instead of
  for every published row; the page still applies the shelf rule itself.
- Tests: server/posts-listing.test.ts runs the real production handler
  (no database, static library) and the dev router on the same listing and
  checks they agree; essay-shelf.test.tsx checks what /writing sends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
